    "D": "126\n\nOfficial Ans. by NTA (B)\nAns. (B)\nSol. $\\mathrm{A}=\\{1,2,3,4\\}$\n$\\mathrm{B}=\\{1,2,3,4,5,6\\}$\nHere f(3) can be 2, 3, 4, 5, 6\n$\\mathrm{f}(3)=2,(\\mathrm{f}(1), \\mathrm{f}(2)) \\rightarrow(1,1) \\rightarrow 6$ cases\n$\\mathrm{f}(3)=3,(\\mathrm{f}(1), \\mathrm{f}(2)) \\rightarrow(1,2),(2,1)$\n$\\rightarrow 2 \\times 6=12$ cases\n$\\mathrm{f}(3)=4,(\\mathrm{f}(1), \\mathrm{f}(2)) \\rightarrow(1,3),(3,1),(2,2)$\n$\\rightarrow 3 \\times 6=18$ cases\n$\\mathrm{f}(3)=5,(\\mathrm{f}(1), \\mathrm{f}(2)) \\rightarrow(1,4),(4,1),(2,3),(3,2)$\n$\\rightarrow 4 \\times 6=24$ cases\n$\\mathrm{f}(3)=6,(\\mathrm{f}(1), \\mathrm{f}(2)) \\rightarrow(1,5),(5,1),(2,4),(4,2),(3,3)$\n$\\rightarrow 5 \\times 6=30$ cases\nTotal number of cases $=6+12+18+24+30=90$\n2. If $\\alpha, \\beta, \\gamma, \\delta$ are the roots of the equation $\\mathrm{x}^{4}+\\mathrm{x}^{3}+\\mathrm{x}^{2}+\\mathrm{x}+1=0$, then\n$\\alpha^{2021}+\\beta^{2021}+\\gamma^{2021}+\\delta^{2021}$ is equal to .\n(A) -4\n(B) -1\n(C) 1\n(D) 4\n\nOfficial Ans. by NTA (B)\nAns. (B)\nSol. $\\alpha, \\beta, \\gamma, \\delta$ root of the equation\n$x^{4}+x^{3}+x^{2}+x+1=0$\nWhich are $5^{\\text {th }}$ roots of unity except 1 .\nthen $\\alpha^{2021}+\\beta^{2021}+\\gamma^{2021}+\\delta^{2021}=$\n$\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma+\\delta=-1$\n3. For $\\mathrm{n} \\in \\mathrm{N}$, let $\\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{n}}=\\left\\{\\mathrm{z} \\in \\mathrm{C}:|\\mathrm{z}-3+2 \\mathrm{i}|=\\frac{\\mathrm{n}}{4}\\right\\}$ and $\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{n}}=\\left\\{\\mathrm{z} \\in \\mathrm{C}:|\\mathrm{z}-2+3 \\mathrm{i}|=\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}}\\right\\}$.\n\nThen the number of elements in the set $\\left\\{\\mathrm{n} \\in \\mathrm{N}: \\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{n}} \\cap \\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{n}}=\\phi\\right\\}$ is :\n(A) 0\n(B) 2\n(C) 3\n(D) 4\n\nOfficial Ans. by NTA (D)\nAns. (Bonus)\nSol. $\\quad \\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{n}}:|\\mathrm{z}-(3-2 \\mathrm{i})|=\\frac{\\mathrm{n}}{4}$ is a circle center $\\mathrm{C}_{1}(3,-2)$\nand radius n/4\n$\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{n}}:|\\mathrm{z}-(2-3 \\mathrm{i})|=\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}}$ is a circle center $\\mathrm{C}_{2}(2,-3)$\nand radius 1/n\nHere $\\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{n}} \\cap \\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{n}}=\\phi$\nBoth circles do not intersect each other\nCase-1: $\\mathrm{C}_{1} \\mathrm{C}_{2}>\\mathrm{n} / 4+1 / \\mathrm{n}$\n$\\sqrt{2}>\\frac{\\mathrm{n}}{4}+\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}}$\nthen $\\mathrm{n}=1,2,3,4$\nCase-2 : $\\mathrm{C}_{1} \\mathrm{C}_{2}<\\left|\\frac{\\mathrm{n}}{4}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}}\\right|$\n$\\Rightarrow \\sqrt{2}<\\left|\\frac{\\mathrm{n}^{2}-4}{4 \\mathrm{n}}\\right|$\n⇒ n has infinite solutions for $\\mathrm{n} \\in \\mathbf{N}$\n4. The number of $\\theta \\in(0,4 \\pi)$ for which the system of linear equations\n$3(\\sin 3 \\theta) x-y+z=2$\n$3(\\cos 2 \\theta) x+4 y+3 z=3$\n$6 x+7 y+7 z=9$\nhas no solution is :\n(A) 6\n(B) 7\n(C) 8\n(D) 9\n\nOfficial Ans. by NTA (B)\nAns. (B)\n\nJEE Exam Solution\nwww.esaral.com\n1"
